From c89b6771963c41075a3f5d38e6777c065e9fe353 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 09:42:33 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] GS: count GIF packet payloads once, at termination

The runtime's sceGifPk* helpers rewrote the open DMA tag's inline QWC on every append. Soulcalibur III mixes the HLE sceGifPkAddGsAD/sceGifPkCloseGifTag with its own sceGifPkTerminate, which adds the payload length to the tag: its movie chain began with CNT 6 instead of 3 and ran into GIF data as DMA tags.

The shared builder helpers now take the count mode explicitly. The GIF builder counts once at termination, adding like the guest terminate; the VIF1 builder keeps its count live while appending, as before (the existing VIF1 test expects that).

Test: a CNT tag with two HLE A+D pairs gets QWC 2 from a guest-style terminate and from the HLE terminate, also when terminated twice; fails on the previous runtime.
---
 ps2xRuntime/src/lib/Kernel/Stubs/GS.cpp | 122 ++++++++++++++----------
 ps2xTest/src/ps2_gs_tests.cpp           |  62 ++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 131 insertions(+), 53 deletions(-)

